WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.859
So I think diversity has gotten a lot of
great, you know,

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:09.300
now empirical evidence that shows that
it generally works in groups, especially

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.160
in organizations and companies. But
here's the fascinating piece of it: For

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.130
companies that have a diversity and
inclusion program globally only, 8% of

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:25.830
them have expanded that beyond gender,
race, sexual orientation, and whatever

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:32.520
else, to include age. So age is not often
thought of in the diversity realm. How

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.660
it's different - STEWART BRAND: Do you want it to be? CONLEY:  I absolutely want it to be, and I think one

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.739
element of it is, you know, cognitive
diversity, which sometimes can be neuro -

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:45.120
how your brain works - but also,
cognitive diversity speaks to what your

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.289
experience in life is. And so I
actually think one of the beauties and

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:53.670
one of the few -  Europe has done a lot
more testing and studies on age

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.809
diversity than the US has, interestingly.
Partly because Europe is aging faster, and

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:01.800
places like Germany have actually had
to do this. What they've actually been

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.600
able to show is that age diversity has a
particularly interesting phenomena

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:12.990
relative to race or gender diversity, in
that gender diversity means

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:18.930
better collaborative skills, for sure.
But what age diversity offers is more

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.500
synthetic thinking, more of what I talked
about earlier: that ability to get the

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.150
gist of something and not to move too
quickly. So what they showed in a major

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.850
German study was a young team all by
itself makes decisions

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:37.560
quickly, and makes a lot of mistakes. An
older team, just older people, takes a

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.549
long time and makes fewer mistakes. When
you mix them together you get the best

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:48.329
of both worlds. And that's what age
diversity can offer the the

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:52.450
organizational world. BRAND: Brilliant, thank you.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.000
 

